WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.871
Task statement 2.2.

2
00:00:01.871 --> 00:00:05.552
Implement structured error responses for MCP tools.

3
00:00:05.552 --> 00:00:15.007
When a billing lookup fails mid-conversation, the error message decides whether the agent retries, asks the customer, or escalates.

4
00:00:16.407 --> 00:00:18.125
Start with a mindset shift.

5
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:20.988
A failed tool call is not the end of the run.

6
00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:25.697
It is a message back to Claude, and Claude reads it like any other result.

7
00:00:25.697 --> 00:00:28.115
The isError flag says the call failed.

8
00:00:28.115 --> 00:00:34.924
The text you put next to it decides whether Claude retries, changes its input, asks the user, or hands off.

9
00:00:36.324 --> 00:00:39.714
Four kinds of failure need four different reactions.

10
00:00:39.714 --> 00:00:41.343
A timeout can be retried.

11
00:00:41.343 --> 00:00:43.690
Bad input needs corrected arguments.

12
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.927
A policy refusal or a permission problem should never be retried.

13
00:00:47.927 --> 00:00:53.924
So return a small structured payload with a category, a retryable flag, and a plain message.

14
00:00:53.924 --> 00:01:02.137
Note that the MCP spec only defines the isError flag; the category and retry fields are your own convention inside the result.

15
00:01:03.537 --> 00:01:06.990
A very common bug is treating no results as a failure.

16
00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.784
If the database answered and found nothing, that is a valid, useful answer.

17
00:01:11.784 --> 00:01:15.045
If the database was unreachable, that is a failure.

18
00:01:15.045 --> 00:01:23.420
Keep the two apart, or the agent will either retry forever or tell a customer they have no orders when really the lookup never ran.

19
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.154
In the research system, a subagent's search times out.

20
00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:32.290
Because the error is transient, the subagent retries locally first.

21
00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:36.796
If it still fails, it should not hide the problem or throw away its work.

22
00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:42.785
It returns the partial results together with a clear error: what was tried, what failed, and why.

23
00:01:42.785 --> 00:01:45.748
Now the coordinator can make an informed choice.

24
00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:48.776
Watch for these patterns.

25
00:01:48.776 --> 00:01:56.914
Generic messages, blanket retries, empty results flagged as errors, and failures that kill the whole run are all distractors.

26
00:01:56.914 --> 00:02:07.265
The exam's answer gives the agent enough structure to choose a sensible recovery: retry what is transient, explain what is final, and keep any partial results.

27
00:02:08.665 --> 00:02:09.223
To recap.

28
00:02:09.223 --> 00:02:14.735
Mark failures with isError, classify them, and say plainly what happened and what to try.

29
00:02:14.735 --> 00:02:17.212
Never confuse no results with a failure.

30
00:02:17.212 --> 00:02:27.183
Recover from transient problems close to where they happen, and pass everything else upward with the partial results attached, so the agent above you can decide.

